Our client is an international public affairs agency located in Brussels. 

Jobomschrijving

Do you have experience in working as an Office Manager in an international environment? Are you fluent in French and English? We have the right job for you! 

We are looking for an Office Manager (m/f/x) for one of our clients in Brussels. 

As Office Manager (m/f/x), you would be responsible for:

Perform administrative tasks for the office, e.g. relations with suppliers, organisation of office meetings and client visits;

Assist with onboarding of new staff;

Manage holiday plans and absences;

Contribute to website and social media channels;

Create content for clients’ websites and social media channels;

Handle invoices;

Liaise with external accountants to process invoices;

Produce expenditure reports;

Prepare content for client meetings, seminars and other events;

Other tasks: Ad-hoc support to client-related activities.

The successful candidate will be an experienced professional who demonstrates the following experiences and competencies:

Relevant degree

At least 2-3 years of working experience in similar positions

Full proficiency (writing and speaking) in English and French (an additional language is an asset);

Very good IT skills (e.g. command of MS Office, incl. in particular Excel, Powerpoint) Desirable

Strong organisational skills

Hard-working and flexible

Eye to detail; result-orientation

Our client is an internationally recognised luxury fashion brand with an established presence across the BeNeLux. As the organisation continues to evolve its HR processes and systems, it is looking for an experienced freelance HR Talent Acquisition professional to strengthen its local HR team in Brussels.

Jobomschrijving

As a Freelance Talent Acquisition professional your responsibilities are:

• Develop and manage job postings to attract qualified candidates ;
• Screen resumes and shortlist potential candidates ;
• Coordinate and conduct interviews with hiring managers ;
• Utilise multiple sourcing channels to identify top talent ;
• Maintain accurate recruitment records and documentation ;
• Provide regular updates to stakeholders on recruitment progress ;
• Support on ad-hoc projects of changing social secretary & ERP systems ;
• Ensure a positive candidate experience throughout the hiring process ;
• Support the onboarding process for new hires ;

A successful Freelance Talent Acquisition professional should have:

• Experience in recruitment, preferably in the Retail industry ;
• Strong knowledge of sourcing techniques and recruitment tools - Workday & SDworkx is a big plus ;
• Ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritise effectively ;
• Excellent communication and interpersonal skills ;
• Attention to detail and strong organisational skills ;
• Proficiency in English & French, Dutch being an asset ;

